  "verbalization": "Phellandral, (R)- is consistently identified as a target of multiple compounds, including Kutzneride 9 and 2-(5-Hydroxy-1H-Indol-3-Yl)Acetic Acid, which in turn target the Prostaglandin E2 receptor EP4 subtype. This suggests a potential mechanism of action involving the regulation of the EP4 receptor, possibly through modulation of its signaling pathways. The evidence is supported by a shared target relationship across three distinct compounds, all of which are implicated in the inhibition of the EP4 receptor. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Phellandral, (R)- and the EP4 receptor, suggesting that the drug may act through a mechanism that involves the EP4 receptor. The mechanism is further supported by the presence of a third compound, which is a more complex molecule, but still targets the same receptor, indicating that the relationship is robust and not limited to a single class of compounds. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Phellandral, (R)- may exert its effects by interacting with the EP4 receptor, potentially through a mechanism that involves the inhibition of its signaling pathways.",
